#8122
The Road to Palanthas~
  The long road to Palanthas runs east-west here. The road is made of
finely crushed cobble and gravel, giving it a fine texture which is 
easier on caravan horse's shodden hooves. To the north a large camp of
tents and makeshift houses stands, thin wisps of smoke rising into the 
air from the many campfires. Though the highway is littered with tracks
and usually well travelled, it is strangely empty and quiet.
~
