#8150
A Pleasant-Looking Cottage~
   Two small, roughly-cut windows allow the only light into this meager
cottage.  The bare floorboards, and rickety chairs lend themselves to
the fact that the owners of this house really don't have a lot to spend.
Still, everything has been kept imaculately clean, and the fire in the
stone fireplace is very warm, and inviting.  Clearly, though these people
are not rich, they are still devoted to love and goodness, as their shrine
to Paladine, a small wooden statue of the patron of paladins resting on
the mantlepiece, shows.
~
81 0 0 0 0 1 255 0
D2
You can see the freshly graveled road of Crown Street from here.
~
~
0 0 8159
S
#8151
A Nicely Kept House~
   Not as glamourous as those on Rose Street, this smaller home still
carries the welcoming sense of comfort in it.  Two easy chairs that look
a little worn with age, but still clean and very inviting sit, each in
a corner facing the red brick fireplace of the small living room.  Though
no carpet is on the floor, the wooden floorboards are smoothly sanded
and painted in soft tones.  And, as is customary in Palanthas, a small
painting -a meager shrine to Paladine- adorns the mantlepiece.
~
