#8154
Crown Street~
   As you step off of Rose Street onto Crown street, the cobblestones fall
away to a freshly graveled road, somewhat narrower,  but still bustling
with people to and fro.  You soon come to realize that Crown Street contains
a somewhat less wealthy class of people.  Although the houses are still
finely built, and almost as large, the artwork and metalwork adorning the
outside of the houses on Rose Street are missing.  Instead, the outer walls
have simply been whitewashed.  Also, you realize that the street names,
and accompanying levels of social classes on each, seem to reflect that
of the three orders of the Solamnic Knights: Rose, Crown, and Sword.
~
