#8158
The Audience Chamber of Lord Amothus~
   This large atrium was built for two reasons: to impress, and to
provide an acoustically sound hearing chamber (rumor has it that Amothus
is going deaf). In the east wall stands the Speaker's chair, where Lord
Amothus sits and listens to the ideas and opinions of Palanthians whom
he has granted an audience. On the north and southern walls are lines of
dark wood chairs and desks for the city council which meets weekly.
This whole room has been crafted decadently, no expense spared. Which
for the same reason it was constructed 'Kender-Proof'. That is, 
everything is securely fastened.
~
81 520 0 0 0 1 255 0
D1
A small door of mahogony is set in the corner of the east wall.
~
door wood mahogony~
1 8153 8173
D2
A sturdy looking, steel-reinforced door of oak makes any unwanted
intrusion into the southern chamber impossible.
~
door oak steel~
2 8152 8172
D3
A grandiose, leather-covered door leads back to the waiting room.
~
door leather~
