#8172
The Planning Chamber and Map Room~
   This large room is where Amothus consults with his military advisors
and most important visitors to discuss and strategize about the Dragonwar
which is spreading farther each day. A large planning table covered in
maps and markers dominated the centre of the room. A large window lies
in the south wall, overlooking all of Palanthas.
~
81 616 0 0 0 1 255 0
D0
This thick, oaken door secures this room from any disturbances.
~
door oaken steel~
2 8152 8158
E
table planning map~
The maps and tables show the positioning of the evil and good 
Dragonarmies across the plains of Solamnia. Dominant features of the 
main map are: Palanthas, the High Clerists Tower, Daargard Keep, and the
main bulk of the Red Dragonarmy.
~
E
window~
   From here, Lord Amothus can look out over his city, which he does
often. With its clean buildings of white marble, bustling streets, and
lush gardens, it looks a city blessed by the Gods themselves.
~
S
#8173
Amothus' Living Quarters~
  This sparsely furnished bedchamber is where Amothus spends most of his
nights (most). A nice four-post bed occupies the centre of the room and
is flanked by a small nightstand and armoire. The north wall is a walk-in
closet where Amothus stores his hundreds of combinations of the latest
and trendiest fashions. In the southeast corner is another staircase, 
which leads down to the living quarters and kitchens.
~
