door wooden mahogony~
1 8153 8158
S
#8174
Gold Wyrm's Lair~
   As you enter the cavernous lair, carved into the mountain by the gold wyrm
himself, you are almost blinded by a shimmering, white light.  As your eyes
adjust, you look towards its source, squinting through the still almost
unbearable light, to see the biggest Gold Dragon you've ever seen.  Then you
look past him, briefly, to take in the rest of his home.  You see, carved into
the northern wall, what looks to be rows upon rows of shelves full of books. 
To your left, in a small alcove, are the treasures he has collected in his
centuries of acting as a bane to evil.  And to your right, you see a HUGE
tapestry, almost as tall as the sixty-foot dragon, portraying a gigantic
flying city with stream upon stream of wyverns flying from it, only to be
destroyed by the mass of good dragons.  Then you lock eyes with the Wyrm, and
you get a feeling in the back of your mind.  But you can't quite tell yet if
it's awe...or fear.
~
81 520 0 0 0 1 255 0
D2
You see a small road leading through the humongous structures that house the dragons.
~
~
0 0 8192
S
#8175
Market Way~
   As you walk down Market way, you can hear the familiar sounds of merchants
and traders trying to sell their goods.  You can smell the tantalizing aroma
of freshly baked bread coming from the bakery, as you take in the rest of the
scene.  Dodging your way through the many street vendors, you catch glimpses
of the many, more permanent shops lining the street.  You see a jeweler trying
to dazzle the crowd with her many fine gems, an armorsmith hammering away in
the open air, a weaponsmith eagerly testing his craftmanship in a friendly
deul with a patron, and a happy mage displaying his mystic inventory before
the crowd.  The only thing missing from this all-too-common scene, you notice
as you look around, is the complete lack of those lesser denizens of the
marketplace, who find their wealth in the purses of others.
~
81 0 0 0 0 1 255 0
